ty_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 5, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`fee(order) -> int` is now in `shipping.py`, with each of the 9 steps implemented in order. I checked it against 24 cases where I worked out the expected amount by hand, and all of them match. The cases cover box splitting, partial weight units, free shipping on the mainland and the islands, both coupons, member discounts, the weekend and fragile surcharges, peak season, rounding up to 10 won, and an unknown region raising `ValueError`. The check script is in the scratchpad, so no test file was added to the project.\n\nThree parts of the spec could be read more than one way. Here is how I handled them:\n\n- **Discount rounding (steps 5 and 6):** I round the discount amount down, then subtract it from the fee. Rounding the discounted fee down instead can differ by 1 won (e.g. gold on 4,150 won gives 3,113 won my way, 3,112 won the other way). Step 9 rounds up to 10 won, so the final amount almost never changes.\n- **Island free shipping (step 4):** I read \"기본 요금 중 최저값\" as the lowest base fee in the whole table, gyeonggi's 3,500 won. So Jeju and Ulleung get 3,500 won off per box.\n- **Unknown member grade:** the spec says nothing about this. I made it raise `ValueError`, the same as an unknown region.\n\nSTATUS: DONE", "ttft_ms": 1376, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 43119, "uuid": "451ce974-fcb0-44f2-9ebb-9a29a3b7a4f4", "ttft_stream_ms": 911, "time_to_request_ms": 237, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 14, "system_prompt": 20, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 1, "input_attachments": 3, "input_hooks": 2, "transcript_persist": 17, "tool_pool_refresh": 1, "init_message": 3, "engine_pickup": 1, "message_prep": 1, "model_config_wait": 0, "autocompact": 1, "query_setup": 0, "model_gates": 160, "tool_schema_build": 7, "message_normalization": 0, "client_creation": 3, "request_build": 3}, "turn_start_resume_kind": "none", "process_turn_index": 0, "time_